# Model placement

Three homes — **do not duplicate** types across them.

## Features (`WebApp/Features/`)

**Slice DTOs** (`DTOs.cs`) — shared read shapes within one slice:

| Folder | Types |
|--------|-------|
| `Users/` | `SessionDto` |
| `ChatThreads/` | `ChatThreadDto` |
| `ChatMessages/` | `ChatMessageDto` |
| `UserSettings/` | `GeneralSettingsDto`, `EmailSettingsDto` |
| `Shared/` | Cross-slice DTOs |

`FromEntity(Core.Entities.*)` for mapping; `AsResponse<T>()` when Response inherits the DTO.

**Use-case types** (`Commands|Queries/{UseCase}.cs`):

| Kind | Pattern |
|------|---------|
| Message | `{UseCase}Request` |
| Result | `{UseCase}Response` (may extend slice DTO) |
| Validator | `{UseCase}RequestValidator` |
| Handler | `{UseCase}RequestHandler` |

Flat Request records; non-nullable Response on `ICommand<T>` / `IQuery<T>` — failures use `HasError`, not null payload.

Do **not** put use-case types in `Core/DTOs/` or `WebApp/Models/`.

## Core (`Core/DTOs/`) — integration only

| File | Types |
|------|-------|
| `Mail.cs` | `InboxQuery`, `MailboxStatusResult`, … |
| `Foundry.cs` | `FoundryOptions` |

No repository or feature DTOs here.

## WebApp (`WebApp/Models/`) — app shell

| File | Types |
|------|-------|
| `Enums.cs` | `SettingsSection` |
| `AI.cs` | `RunChatAgentRequest/Response` |
| `Constants.cs` | `AuthConstants`, `ChatMessageRoles` |

## Decision tree

1. Single use-case pair? → Features file
2. Shared read shape in one slice? → `Features/{Slice}/DTOs.cs`
3. Shared across slices? → `Features/Shared/DTOs.cs`
4. Mailbox / Foundry port? → `Core/DTOs/`
5. `Result` / `ErrorCode`? → `MediatR.Results`
6. AI turn shapes? → `WebApp/Models/AI.cs`
7. DB entity? → `Core/Entities/`

## Layer flow

| Direction | Pattern |
|-----------|---------|
| UI → Features | `Mediator.SendAsync(new SignInRequest(...))` |
| Handlers → repos | `{entity}Repo` + `sharedRepo` |
| Repos → handlers | Slice DTOs |
| UI lists | May bind slice DTOs directly |

Handler/repo conventions: **`feature-slice-conventions.mdc`**.
